# Response headers for the Cloudflare-hosted build. Vite copies public/ to the
# root of dist/, which is where Cloudflare parses this file. It is consumed as
# configuration, never served as an asset.
#
# This file replaces the seven `gsutil setmeta` calls that used to apply the
# same policy imperatively after each GCS sync (issue #1713). Everything the
# old pipeline set is reproduced below; nothing else was set.
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO _redirects FILE. The obvious SPA rule
# `/*  /index.html  200` is wrong here: Cloudflare documents that "Redirects
# are always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the
# incoming request", so a catch-all would shadow every hashed asset, the
# service worker, and the AASA file with the HTML shell. It is also
# unnecessary — dist/ has no top-level 404.html, which is exactly the
# condition under which Cloudflare falls back to the SPA entrypoint on its
# own. vite.config.test.ts pins both halves of that.
#
# Two matching quirks drive the rule shapes below:
#   1. Duplicate header names across matching rules are JOINED WITH A COMMA,
#      not overridden. A Cache-Control under /* would corrupt every rule below
#      it into "no-store, public, max-age=31536000, immutable". /* therefore
#      carries the one header that is genuinely global and appears nowhere
#      else.
#   2. /index.html is redirected to / before it is served, so a rule keyed on
#      /index.html only ever decorates that redirect. The app shell has to be
#      pinned on "/".

# Replaces the HSTS header the production webpage load balancer emitted via
# google_compute_backend_bucket.custom_response_headers, which goes away with
# the LB. Applied on staging too, deliberately: staging is the rehearsal for
# the production cutover, and an unproven header is the whole reason this is
# here. trackrat.net is NOT currently on the browser preload list, so the
# `preload` token is a statement of intent rather than a live commitment.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload

# Content-hashed filenames: a rebuild emits a new name rather than mutating an
# existing one, so these can never go stale in a client cache.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The app shell. Keyed on "/" and not "/index.html" — see quirk 2 above.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

# vite-plugin-pwa (workbox) output. A cached service worker pins itself and
# every client that registered it, so these two must always be refetched.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/registerSW.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

# Apple requires application/json for Universal Links. The file has no
# extension, so Cloudflare cannot infer the type from it.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json
